DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The QQ__QQAADDDDII(), QQ__QQDDIIVVII(), QQ__QQMMUULLII() and QQ__QQSSUUBBII() functions add, divide,
     multiply or subtract _b to/by/from _a respectively, storing the result in
     _a.

     The QQ__QQFFRRAACCII() function computes the fraction _n divided by _d and stores
     the fixed-point result in _q.

     The QQ__QQCCPPYYVVAALLII() function overwrites _q's integer and fractional bits with
     the Q representation of integer value _i.

     All of those functions operate on the following data types: _s_8_q___t, _u_8_q___t,
     _s_1_6_q___t, _u_1_6_q___t, _s_3_2_q___t, _u_3_2_q___t, _s_6_4_q___t, and _u_6_4_q___t, which are referred to
     generically as _Q_T_Y_P_E.  The _I_T_Y_P_E refers to the stdint(7) integer types.

     For more details, see qmath(3).

